  "abstract": "Classical compact-support suspension theory yields a smooth foliated surface-times-interval with product endpoint collars and nonzero Godbillon–Vey integral. We place arbitrarily many copies inside one fixed pseudo-Anosov mapping torus. One embedded closed transversal meets every leaf, and the Godbillon–Vey numbers grow linearly with the number of copies. This gives a negative answer to the unrestricted volume-bound question printed as Question 10.6 in Calegari’s 2002 manuscript. The construction uses classical ingredients; historical priority of this specific consequence remains unestablished.",
